Subject: [PATCH] ApplicationPlay: play a Blu-ray's menu when it is asked for

A Blu-ray's listing offers a Menu entry, a bluray:// path ending in
"menu", and libbluray plays that path in navigation mode. Before playing
any bluray:// path, GetMenuDecisions() applies the disc playback setting
to it. With "play main title" it finds the main title and plays that
playlist instead, and with "show simplified menu" it shows the playlist
selection again, so the disc menu can only be reached by setting the
whole player to "show disc menu". Playing the main title out of
navigation mode also leaves the menu key without anything to open:
CDVDInputStreamBluray::OnMenu() logs "navigation mode not enabled".

A menu path is now played as it comes. "Choose playlist" from the
context menu still shows the selection.

Signed-off-by: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
---
diff --git a/xbmc/application/ApplicationPlay.cpp b/xbmc/application/ApplicationPlay.cpp
index 3ffbab621d..4b11cf82ef 100644
--- a/xbmc/application/ApplicationPlay.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/application/ApplicationPlay.cpp
@@ -210,6 +210,10 @@ MenuDecision GetMenuDecisions(const CFileItem& item,
   if (forceSelectionAlways && isBlurayPath)
     return SHOW_SIMPLE_MENU;
 
+  // The disc menu was asked for, so it is what plays, whatever the setting would pick
+  if (URIUtils::IsBlurayMenuPath(item.GetDynPath()))
+    return NO_ACTION;
+
   // Show Disc menu
   // This takes priority over the simple menu
   const bool useDiscMenuSetting{playbackSetting == BD_PLAYBACK_DISC_MENU};
